  "definition": "ADHD is a childhood-onset behavior disorder marked by developmentally inappropriate inattention, impulsivity, and hyperactivity. Some people mainly show inattention or mainly hyperactivity-impulsivity, and while symptoms often lessen by late adolescence, some continue into adulthood.",
